on of this scanner)\",\r\n98:      r\"[A-Za-z0-9+/]{120,}={0,2}\")\r\n99: rule(\"obfuscation\", \"opaque\",\r\n100:      \"zero-width or bidirectional unicode control chars (hidden text)\",\r\n101:      r\"[​‌‍⁠‪-‮⁦-⁩]\")\r\n102: \r\n103: # --- ELEVATED: privilege, secrets, destruction. The \"read my passwords\" /\r\n104: #     \"survives reboot\" class. Forces T3. (Persistence is context-aware — see\r\n105: #     the CONFIG/WRITE/HOME regexes and the scan loop below.) ---\r\n106: # STRUCTURAL, language-independent signals only. To make an agent touch a\r\n107: # credential the skill must name the PATH (universal across languages and\r\n108: # phrasings), or hardcode the secret inline. Bare prose words like \"password\"\r\n109: # are NOT matched — enumerating verbs in one language is a losing game and\r\n110: # blind to paraphrase/other languages. Prose intent (\"read the user's keys\",\r\n111: # in any language) is the AGENT layer's job, not the regex's.\r\n112: rule(\"secrets\", \"elevated\",\r\n113:      \"references credential/secret file locations\",\r\n114:      r\"(?:\\.aws/|\\.ssh/|id_rsa|id_ed25519|\\.netrc|\\.npmrc|\\.env\\b|\\.pgpass|\"\r\n115:      r\"\\.git-credentials|/etc/shadow|keychain|GITHUB_TOKEN|AWS_SECRET)\")\r\n116: rule(\"secrets\", \"elevated\",\r\n117:      \"hardcoded secret assigned inline\",\r\n118:      r\"(?:password|secret|api[_-]?key|access[_-]?token|auth[_-]?token)\"\r\n119:      r\"s?\\s*[=:]\\s*[\\\"']?[\\w./+-]{8,}\")\r\n120: rule(\"destructive\", \"elevated\",\r\n121:      \"destructive filesystem or disk command\",\r\n122:      r\"(?:\\brm\\s+-rf?\\b|\\bdd\\s+if=|\\bmkfs\\b|\u003e\\s*/dev/sd|chmod\\s+-R?\\s*777|\"\r\n123:      r\"\\bshred\\b|:\\(\\)\\s*\\{\\s*:\\|:)\")\r\n124: rule(\"privilege\", \"elevated\",\r\n125:      \"escalates privileges\",\r\n126:      r\"\\bsudo\\b|\\bdoas\\b|\\bsu\\s+-\\b|osascript.*administrator\")\r\n127: rule(\"exfil\", \"elevated\",\r\n128:      \"raw socket / netcat (possible exfiltration channel